1
00:00:37,184 --> 00:00:38,264
Trees

2
00:00:38,424 --> 00:00:43,463
surely among the
most magnificent of all living things

3
00:00:45,822 --> 00:00:49,062
Some are the
largest organisms on Earth

4
00:00:49,102 --> 00:00:51,102
dwarfing
all others

5
00:00:51,142 --> 00:00:54,621
And these are the
tallest of them all

6
00:01:07,804 --> 00:01:13,530
The deciduous and coniferous woodlands that grow in the seasonal parts of our planet

7
00:01:13,570 --> 00:01:16,893
are the most
extensive forests on Earth

8
00:01:25,593 --> 00:01:29,754
Their sheer
extent stuns the imagination

9
00:01:42,237 --> 00:01:45,117
The barren
snows of the Arctic

10
00:01:45,157 --> 00:01:47,958
A thousand miles
from the North Pole

11
00:01:47,998 --> 00:01:49,918
And heading south

12
00:01:53,016 --> 00:01:57,021
This is the very
first place the trees can grow

13
00:01:59,585 --> 00:02:00,506
To begin with

14
00:02:00,546 --> 00:02:02,468
the conifers are sparse

15
00:02:02,549 --> 00:02:03,590
But soon

16
00:02:03,630 --> 00:02:05,712
they dominate the land

17
00:02:14,284 --> 00:02:17,447
This is the
tiger forest

18
00:02:19,438 --> 00:02:21,521
There are as
many trees here

19
00:02:21,561 --> 00:02:25,126
as in all the
world's rainforests combined

20
00:02:26,328 --> 00:02:28,692
The tiger
circles the globe

21
00:02:28,732 --> 00:02:32,336
and contains a
third of all the trees on Earth

22
00:02:32,497 --> 00:02:34,901
It produces
so much oxygen

23
00:02:34,941 --> 00:02:39,306
that it refreshes
the atmosphere of the entire planet

24
00:02:44,025 --> 00:02:46,465
At the tiger's
northern extent

25
00:02:46,505 --> 00:02:51,066
the growing season can last for just one month a year

26
00:02:51,827 --> 00:02:56,627
It can take 50 years for a tree to get bigger than a seedling

27
00:03:10,529 --> 00:03:12,809
It's a
silent world

28
00:03:12,850 --> 00:03:14,730
where little stirs

29
00:03:16,810 --> 00:03:20,091
But there are
occasional signs of life

30
00:03:20,131 --> 00:03:22,731
stories
written in the snow

31
00:03:24,291 --> 00:03:26,812
The prints of
an Arctic fox

32
00:03:27,092 --> 00:03:29,972
and the hare it
might have been stalking

33
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:37,340
A female
polar bear

34
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:39,220
and her two cubs

35
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:52,941
Some animals are
so difficult to glimpse

36
00:03:52,981 --> 00:03:54,941
that they're
like spirits

37
00:03:55,421 --> 00:03:58,301
One could live a
lifetime in these woods

38
00:03:58,621 --> 00:04:00,901
and never
see a lynx

39
00:04:04,523 --> 00:04:08,522
The cat must roam
hundreds of miles in search of prey

40
00:04:08,722 --> 00:04:12,122
And may never
visit the same patch of forest twice

41
00:04:14,401 --> 00:04:17,561
It's the very
essence of wilderness

42
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:25,400
With so few
prey animals here

43
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:28,999
life for a hunter
is particularly hard

44
00:04:31,654 --> 00:04:33,095
Creatures
are scarce

45
00:04:33,135 --> 00:04:36,096
because few can
eat conifer needles

46
00:04:36,937 --> 00:04:39,339
The moose is
an exception

47
00:04:44,543 --> 00:04:46,544
Growth is
so difficult

48
00:04:46,584 --> 00:04:49,146
that conifers
protect their precious leaves

49
00:04:49,186 --> 00:04:51,067
by filling
them with resin

50
00:04:51,107 --> 00:04:53,269
That reduces water loss

51
00:04:53,309 --> 00:04:56,271
but it also makes
them very distasteful

52
00:05:07,389 --> 00:05:11,073
At least the
conifer seeds are edible

53
00:05:11,235 --> 00:05:14,679
But they're
protected within armourplated cones

54
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:17,924
And it takes a
specialist to reach them

55
00:05:20,568 --> 00:05:22,892
The crossbill's
extraordinary beak

56
00:05:22,932 --> 00:05:24,855
can prise
apart the scales

57
00:05:24,895 --> 00:05:28,339
so that its
tongue can extract the seeds

58
00:05:32,138 --> 00:05:33,900
Birds are
fortunate

59
00:05:33,940 --> 00:05:35,821
When the seasonal
crop is gathered

60
00:05:35,861 --> 00:05:37,902
they can fly south

61
00:05:42,587 --> 00:05:47,751
But one animal is
so expert at survival in this frozen forest

62
00:05:47,791 --> 00:05:52,114
that it stays
here and is active all year long

63
00:05:54,824 --> 00:05:56,385
In local folklore

64
00:05:56,425 --> 00:05:59,666
the wolverine is
a link to the spirit world

65
00:05:59,706 --> 00:06:02,546
and a cross
between a bear and a wolf

66
00:06:02,866 --> 00:06:04,187
In reality

67
00:06:04,227 --> 00:06:06,427
it's a
huge weasel

68
00:06:08,908 --> 00:06:11,749
Its bulk helps to
conserve body heat

69
00:06:11,789 --> 00:06:13,829
and also
broadens its menu

70
00:06:13,869 --> 00:06:15,670
It's so big
and powerful

71
00:06:15,710 --> 00:06:19,231
it can even bring
down an adult caribou

72
00:06:21,033 --> 00:06:22,394
For its size

73
00:06:22,434 --> 00:06:26,476
it's said that the animal can eat more in one sitting than any other

74
00:06:26,516 --> 00:06:29,398
which is why it's
also known as the glutton

75
00:06:47,863 --> 00:06:49,745
Being
gluttonous here

76
00:06:49,785 --> 00:06:52,148
is a very
effective strategy

77
00:06:52,188 --> 00:06:54,911
It's wise to
eat all you can

78
00:06:54,951 --> 00:06:56,272
when you can

79
00:06:57,874 --> 00:07:01,038
And when even a
glutton can't eat more

80
00:07:01,078 --> 00:07:03,401
It stores what'
s left for later

81
00:07:03,441 --> 00:07:05,763
in the surrounding deep freeze

82
00:07:13,418 --> 00:07:16,341
Spring in
the ice forest

83
00:07:27,597 --> 00:07:32,122
The kapokayi can
also digest conifer needles

84
00:07:32,403 --> 00:07:36,007
But feeding is
not its priority at the moment

85
00:07:38,538 --> 00:07:39,778
Like gladiators

86
00:07:39,818 --> 00:07:42,297
the males square
up for a battle

87
00:07:42,337 --> 00:07:56,976
Each may have
just a single chance

88
00:07:57,016 --> 00:07:59,176
to impress a female

89
00:08:00,456 --> 00:08:04,296
Neither can
afford a lapse in concentration

90
00:08:29,088 --> 00:08:32,849
The injured
loser may not survive

91
00:08:38,050 --> 00:08:40,819
The inhabitants
of this great wilderness

92
00:08:40,859 --> 00:08:42,384
May live and die

93
00:08:42,424 --> 00:08:45,551
without ever
having contact with humanity

94
00:08:46,075 --> 00:08:48,400
Long may it
be that way

95
00:08:58,452 --> 00:09:02,018
The northern
forests may be the largest on earth

96
00:09:02,058 --> 00:09:06,425
But to see coniferous trees that have reached their full potential

97
00:09:06,465 --> 00:09:09,950
You must travel a
thousand miles south of here

98
00:09:16,041 --> 00:09:18,325
The Pacific coast
of North America

99
00:09:25,232 --> 00:09:27,274
The land
of hemlock

100
00:09:27,314 --> 00:09:28,795
Douglas fir

101
00:09:28,995 --> 00:09:31,197
and giant redwood

102
00:09:39,043 --> 00:09:39,764
Here

103
00:09:39,804 --> 00:09:42,606
water is never
locked up in ice

104
00:09:42,646 --> 00:09:44,608
And even if
rains fail

105
00:09:44,648 --> 00:09:47,971
the needles can
extract moisture from the fogs

106
00:09:48,011 --> 00:09:49,972
That roll in
from the sea

107
00:09:58,407 --> 00:10:01,411
The sun's energy
powers these forests

108
00:10:01,451 --> 00:10:04,413
not for one month
as it does in the taiga

109
00:10:04,454 --> 00:10:06,176
but for
half the year

110
00:10:15,914 --> 00:10:20,719
These conifers grow at ten times the rate of those near the Arctic

111
00:10:20,759 --> 00:10:23,721
And they live
for thousands of years

112
00:10:34,051 --> 00:10:37,094
One grove of
redwoods in California

113
00:10:37,134 --> 00:10:41,097
contains three of
the tallest trees on Earth

114
00:10:46,419 --> 00:10:49,381
This one is over
a hundred metres high

115
00:10:49,421 --> 00:10:52,423
the size of a 30-
storey building

116
00:11:21,012 --> 00:11:26,500
These forests were growing here long before humans walked the earth

117
00:11:26,661 --> 00:11:30,066
They were in
their prime 20 million years ago

118
00:11:30,106 --> 00:11:33,952
And existed before the Swiss Alps or the Rocky Mountains

119
00:11:33,992 --> 00:11:35,834
Were even raised

120
00:11:48,747 --> 00:11:52,869
There is more living matter in a forest of giant conifers

121
00:11:52,909 --> 00:11:55,630
than in any
tropical rainforest

122
00:11:55,711 --> 00:11:58,992
But it's all
contained within the trees

123
00:11:59,393 --> 00:12:03,115
These are as
inedible as those in the tiger

124
00:12:03,155 --> 00:12:05,676
so animals
are still scarce

125
00:12:06,516 --> 00:12:08,357
But they
are present

126
00:12:12,048 --> 00:12:13,649
A pine martin

127
00:12:13,689 --> 00:12:14,971
It's spring

128
00:12:15,011 --> 00:12:16,492
The best
time of year

129
00:12:16,532 --> 00:12:18,693
For a martin
to find food

130
00:12:34,884 --> 00:12:38,289
Bird's eggs are
a seasonal snack

131
00:12:38,329 --> 00:12:39,852
And for a
short time

132
00:12:39,892 --> 00:12:41,613
there's
plenty of them

133
00:12:43,377 --> 00:12:45,939
Sometimes
perhaps too many

134
00:12:49,595 --> 00:12:51,275
But to live
here permanently

135
00:12:51,315 --> 00:12:55,116
the martin needs
a more reliable food source

136
00:12:56,356 --> 00:12:58,637
Squirrels
fit the bill

137
00:12:58,917 --> 00:13:01,517
They thrive here
on the pine cones

138
00:13:01,557 --> 00:13:03,838
And although
these are also seasonal

139
00:13:03,878 --> 00:13:07,399
they can be stored and eaten throughout the year

140
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,680
The squirrels
are busy mating

141
00:13:18,776 --> 00:13:20,537
Good news
for the hunter

142
00:13:20,577 --> 00:13:22,377
A distracted squirrel

143
00:13:22,417 --> 00:13:24,418
is a vulnerable squirrel

144
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:32,581
But this time

145
00:13:32,621 --> 00:13:34,901
the amorous
couple are safe

146
00:13:34,982 --> 00:13:37,583
There is a loner
stocking his larder

147
00:13:37,623 --> 00:13:40,143
who will be
the easier target

148
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:16,640
Early summer

149
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:20,680
and great grey
owl chicks are fledging

150
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:25,919
Adults can only
raise young here

151
00:14:25,959 --> 00:14:30,759
In years when the
seasonal vole crop is big enough to support them

152
00:14:35,639 --> 00:14:39,119
The moment has
arrived for their first flight

153
00:14:44,391 --> 00:14:47,474
Leapin' from the
world's tallest trees

154
00:14:47,514 --> 00:14:49,875
is not for
the fainthearted

155
00:15:16,039 --> 00:15:18,042
If you're
going to fall here

156
00:15:18,082 --> 00:15:21,687
it's quite a good
idea to do it in stages

157
00:15:40,264 --> 00:15:43,909
The ground is no
place for an owl

158
00:15:46,193 --> 00:15:48,998
If he's to climb
to the top of his class

159
00:15:49,038 --> 00:15:51,040
he'll need
to persevere

160
00:15:53,885 --> 00:15:55,006
So now

161
00:15:55,207 --> 00:15:56,849
let's have
another go

162
00:16:17,487 --> 00:16:22,855
The American conifer forests may not be the richest in animal life

163
00:16:23,136 --> 00:16:26,260
But their trees
are extraordinary

164
00:16:26,862 --> 00:16:28,585
This giant sequoia

165
00:16:28,625 --> 00:16:30,468
a relative
of the redwood

166
00:16:30,508 --> 00:16:33,231
is the largest
living thing on earth

167
00:16:33,833 --> 00:16:35,756
Known as
General Sherman

168
00:16:35,796 --> 00:16:38,999
it's the weight
of ten blue whales

169
00:16:49,372 --> 00:16:52,056
Higher up in the
nearby mountains

170
00:16:52,096 --> 00:16:54,058
bristlecone pines

171
00:16:54,098 --> 00:16:57,181
the oldest
organisms on the planet

172
00:16:59,182 --> 00:17:03,063
Some have been
here for five thousand years

173
00:17:03,103 --> 00:17:06,304
They were alive
before the pyramids were built

174
00:17:06,344 --> 00:17:09,185
And were already
three thousand years old

175
00:17:09,225 --> 00:17:11,385
When Christ was born

176
00:17:16,387 --> 00:17:17,827
Across the equator

177
00:17:17,867 --> 00:17:19,708
in the
southern hemisphere

178
00:17:19,748 --> 00:17:23,428
There are forests
that mirror those of the north

179
00:17:24,718 --> 00:17:26,478
Here in
South America

180
00:17:26,518 --> 00:17:29,277
oricaria trees
or monkey puzzles

181
00:17:29,317 --> 00:17:31,877
are like the
conifers of the tiger

182
00:17:32,437 --> 00:17:35,636
They have waterproof scales instead of needles

183
00:17:35,676 --> 00:17:38,155
and their cones
look a little different

184
00:17:38,195 --> 00:17:40,515
but the
principles are the same

185
00:17:45,546 --> 00:17:50,872
Slender billed parakeets rather than crossbills extract their seeds

186
00:17:59,563 --> 00:18:01,806
Where the growing
season is longer

187
00:18:01,846 --> 00:18:03,688
there are
alea trees

188
00:18:03,728 --> 00:18:05,770
the redwoods
of the south

189
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:23,462
As in the
frozen north

190
00:18:23,502 --> 00:18:28,508
the Valdivian
forests of Chile support very few animals

191
00:18:28,548 --> 00:18:31,831
But that is the
end of the similarity

192
00:18:35,408 --> 00:18:39,849
This is a bizarre
world of miniature creatures

193
00:18:42,771 --> 00:18:43,611
The poodoo

194
00:18:43,651 --> 00:18:45,932
the world's
smallest deer

195
00:18:45,972 --> 00:18:49,333
feeds on the
giant leaves of the gunnera plant

196
00:18:57,205 --> 00:19:01,414
The female is
just 30cm high at the shoulder

197
00:19:01,454 --> 00:19:04,580
And her infants
are hardly bigger than kittens

198
00:19:22,236 --> 00:19:24,798
The male
must stay alert

199
00:19:24,838 --> 00:19:26,278
there are
hunters here

200
00:19:26,318 --> 00:19:28,359
who would
snatch his young

201
00:19:30,681 --> 00:19:32,122
Another miniature

202
00:19:32,162 --> 00:19:34,042
the kodkod cat

203
00:19:37,965 --> 00:19:40,927
It's the smallest
cat in all the Americas

204
00:19:40,967 --> 00:19:44,288
And a young
poodle would be a feast for it

205
00:19:45,675 --> 00:19:47,756
But with the
male on guard

206
00:19:47,796 --> 00:19:50,757
the codcod must
lower his sights

207
00:19:56,319 --> 00:19:58,359
Moths are hatching

208
00:19:58,399 --> 00:20:00,400
they're the
last of the summer

209
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:04,161
The tiny cat
should be able to score with these

210
00:20:07,170 --> 00:20:10,370
No one knows why
the creatures here are so small

211
00:20:10,410 --> 00:20:14,130
But at least they
can survive on meagre rations

212
00:20:40,918 --> 00:20:44,845
You might call
this a game of cat and moth

213
00:21:08,966 --> 00:21:11,688
As winter
approaches in Chile

214
00:21:11,728 --> 00:21:15,449
spring is arriving in the northern hemisphere

215
00:21:23,534 --> 00:21:27,776
These are the
deciduous forests of home

216
00:21:28,670 --> 00:21:30,231
Dormant
throughout the winter

217
00:21:30,271 --> 00:21:31,792
they now undergo

218
00:21:31,832 --> 00:21:34,554
one of the most
magical transformations

219
00:21:34,594 --> 00:21:36,354
in the
natural world

220
00:21:48,565 --> 00:21:49,965
By late spring

221
00:21:50,005 --> 00:21:53,885
the landscape is
wrapped in a vibrant fresh green

222
00:21:54,245 --> 00:21:54,845
Here

223
00:21:54,885 --> 00:21:56,284
instead
of conifers

224
00:21:56,324 --> 00:21:58,564
there are
broadleaf trees

225
00:21:58,604 --> 00:22:03,004
And that makes the character of this forest entirely different

226
00:22:07,765 --> 00:22:08,767
Being broad

227
00:22:08,807 --> 00:22:12,493
these leaves
trap much more light than needles

228
00:22:12,574 --> 00:22:14,097
But they'
re also thin

229
00:22:14,137 --> 00:22:16,580
soft， and edible

230
00:22:36,092 --> 00:22:39,414
And others can
eat the leaf eaters

231
00:23:01,801 --> 00:23:02,881
It's spring

232
00:23:02,921 --> 00:23:05,363
in the great
broadleaved forests

233
00:23:05,403 --> 00:23:08,605
of Eastern Europe
and Asiatic Russia

234
00:23:09,967 --> 00:23:12,608
The mandarin
ducks are courtin'

235
00:23:26,350 --> 00:23:30,075
The female
mandarin nests in a tree hole

236
00:23:30,115 --> 00:23:32,878
And when it's
time for everyone to leave

237
00:23:32,918 --> 00:23:34,960
She leads the way

238
00:23:38,005 --> 00:23:41,649
The ducklings are
only 24 hours old

239
00:23:44,173 --> 00:23:45,775
It's a long drop

240
00:23:45,815 --> 00:23:48,858
And a few calls
of encouragement are required

241
00:24:02,299 --> 00:24:03,461
Two down

242
00:24:03,501 --> 00:24:04,941
seven to go

243
00:24:39,583 --> 00:24:41,825
There are
still two missing

244
00:25:03,886 --> 00:25:06,167
All present
and correct

245
00:25:06,908 --> 00:25:10,112
But they won't be
safe until they reach water

246
00:25:10,152 --> 00:25:13,716
And the forest
pool is almost a mile away

247
00:25:49,933 --> 00:25:50,893
By June

248
00:25:50,933 --> 00:25:53,173
the days are
at their longest

249
00:25:53,213 --> 00:25:55,573
And all across
the northern hemisphere

250
00:25:55,613 --> 00:25:58,533
The broad leaves
are hard at work

251
00:26:08,154 --> 00:26:10,276
On the east coast
of North America

252
00:26:10,316 --> 00:26:13,359
it seems like
any other summer's evening

253
00:26:15,722 --> 00:26:18,644
But tonight
is special

254
00:26:22,890 --> 00:26:25,892
After 17
years underground

255
00:26:26,133 --> 00:26:28,655
creatures
are stirring

256
00:26:34,878 --> 00:26:38,162
The nymphs of the
periodical cicada

257
00:26:38,202 --> 00:26:40,244
Have been
biding their time

258
00:26:40,485 --> 00:26:45,170
Now they march
like zombies towards the nearest tree

259
00:26:45,372 --> 00:26:47,213
And start to climb

260
00:26:55,252 --> 00:26:56,213
At first

261
00:26:56,253 --> 00:26:58,374
there are
merely thousands

262
00:26:58,455 --> 00:26:59,416
But soon

263
00:26:59,456 --> 00:27:03,459
more than a
billion swarm all over the forest

264
00:27:03,500 --> 00:27:08,063
The biggest insect emergence on the planet is underway

265
00:27:39,207 --> 00:27:41,449
They invade the
upper branches

266
00:27:41,489 --> 00:27:44,813
Where they climb
out of their external skeletons

267
00:27:44,853 --> 00:27:48,536
And assume their
adult winged form

268
00:27:56,980 --> 00:27:57,741
At first

269
00:27:57,781 --> 00:27:59,822
they're
white and soft

270
00:27:59,862 --> 00:28:03,743
But they have until dawn to complete their transformation

271
00:28:17,948 --> 00:28:20,750
After an
absence of 17 years

272
00:28:20,790 --> 00:28:24,551
The forest is now
overrun by cicadas

273
00:28:32,968 --> 00:28:35,088
The adults
are clumsy

274
00:28:35,328 --> 00:28:37,569
and very edible

275
00:28:46,857 --> 00:28:50,066
For turtles and
other inhabitants of the forest

276
00:28:50,106 --> 00:28:52,473
This is a feast
they're lucky to see

277
00:28:52,513 --> 00:28:54,078
Once in
their lifetime

278
00:28:54,118 --> 00:28:57,124
And they gorge
themselves while they can

279
00:29:10,832 --> 00:29:13,272
Times have
never been so good

280
00:29:13,352 --> 00:29:15,633
The cicadas
have no defences

281
00:29:15,673 --> 00:29:19,113
and virtually
offer themselves to their attackers

282
00:29:29,676 --> 00:29:32,517
The stream of
insects is so relentless

283
00:29:32,557 --> 00:29:37,158
That soon all the
predators are full to the point of bursting

284
00:29:48,758 --> 00:29:51,678
And still the
cicadas come

285
00:29:51,718 --> 00:29:53,837
With the
predators overwhelmed

286
00:29:53,877 --> 00:29:56,997
the survivors can
achieve their purpose

287
00:30:00,236 --> 00:30:01,396
After mating

288
00:30:01,436 --> 00:30:03,718
the adults
lay their eggs

289
00:30:03,758 --> 00:30:05,999
and then
their job is done

290
00:30:06,320 --> 00:30:07,521
In just a few days

291
00:30:07,561 --> 00:30:09,202
they will all die

292
00:30:09,242 --> 00:30:11,603
and the forest
will fall silent

293
00:30:12,004 --> 00:30:15,006
The cicadas here
will not be heard again

294
00:30:15,046 --> 00:30:17,727
for another 17 years

295
00:30:28,028 --> 00:30:29,709
Having fed
the predators

296
00:30:29,749 --> 00:30:32,709
the cicadas
leave one final gift

297
00:30:32,749 --> 00:30:34,829
for the
forest itself

298
00:30:35,109 --> 00:30:37,909
The nutrients in
a generation of cicadas

299
00:30:37,949 --> 00:30:41,149
are returned to
the soil all at once

300
00:30:41,469 --> 00:30:45,269
And the trees
enjoy a marked spurt in growth

301
00:30:45,509 --> 00:30:49,190
This may be the
single largest dose of fertilizer

302
00:30:49,230 --> 00:30:50,950
in the
natural world

303
00:31:12,410 --> 00:31:15,935
In the great
broadleaf forests of Eastern Europe

304
00:31:15,975 --> 00:31:18,378
the days are
beginning to shorten

305
00:31:18,459 --> 00:31:23,586
And a primeval
sound heralds the onset of autumn

306
00:31:42,325 --> 00:31:46,287
Male red deer are
starting their rut

307
00:31:52,091 --> 00:31:55,773
The air is heavy
with the scent of females

308
00:32:07,754 --> 00:32:10,040
The rules
are simple

309
00:32:10,203 --> 00:32:12,127
Winner takes all

310
00:33:06,626 --> 00:33:08,829
Across the
northern hemisphere

311
00:33:08,869 --> 00:33:11,791
the deciduous
forests are changing

312
00:33:12,152 --> 00:33:16,196
Leaves that have
provided food and shelter since the spring

313
00:33:16,237 --> 00:33:17,677
are now shed

314
00:33:22,443 --> 00:33:25,246
In the broadleaf
forests of Russia

315
00:33:25,366 --> 00:33:28,369
winter is
particularly severe

316
00:33:33,707 --> 00:33:35,788
But there will
always be some

317
00:33:35,828 --> 00:33:38,149
who benefit
from hardship

318
00:33:42,512 --> 00:33:45,153
Black vultures
scavenge from the carcass

319
00:33:45,193 --> 00:33:49,275
of a sika deer
that has died of cold or starvation

320
00:33:49,555 --> 00:33:51,997
These endangered
birds are visitors

321
00:33:52,037 --> 00:33:53,798
They've come
down from the north

322
00:33:53,838 --> 00:33:57,599
to escape the
even colder conditions in Siberia

323
00:34:35,271 --> 00:34:37,352
An Amur leopard

324
00:34:37,473 --> 00:34:40,114
the rarest
cat on earth

325
00:34:40,836 --> 00:34:43,959
Winter is a
difficult time for this hunter

326
00:34:43,999 --> 00:34:45,800
There are no
leaves for cover

327
00:34:45,840 --> 00:34:48,242
and no young
prey animals

328
00:34:48,563 --> 00:34:51,005
This female has
the added pressure

329
00:34:51,045 --> 00:34:54,448
of having to
provide for her oneyearold cub

330
00:34:54,729 --> 00:34:56,610
It will be
another twelve months

331
00:34:56,650 --> 00:34:59,452
before he'll be
able to fend for himself

332
00:35:12,502 --> 00:35:16,425
The bickering
vultures have abandoned the carcass

333
00:35:16,706 --> 00:35:20,029
It's a valuable
discovery for the leopards

334
00:35:25,114 --> 00:35:29,598
But the cub doesn'
t share its mother's sense of urgency

335
00:35:59,473 --> 00:36:03,434
The vultures have
left behind plenty of good meat

336
00:36:03,595 --> 00:36:06,036
But it's
stiff with frost

337
00:36:08,425 --> 00:36:10,905
The mother works
to open the hide

338
00:36:10,945 --> 00:36:14,145
And make feeding
a little easier for her cub

339
00:36:25,784 --> 00:36:30,184
There are only 40
Amur leopards left in the wild

340
00:36:32,504 --> 00:36:35,344
And that number
is still falling

341
00:36:36,417 --> 00:36:38,621
The harshness of
the winter here

342
00:36:38,661 --> 00:36:41,305
hinders their
increase in numbers

343
00:36:41,346 --> 00:36:43,430
It takes one of
these females longer

344
00:36:43,470 --> 00:36:45,714
to raise her
young to independence

345
00:36:45,754 --> 00:36:48,318
than it does a
leopard in Africa

346
00:36:56,289 --> 00:37:00,654
If the mother can
sustain her cub for a few more weeks

347
00:37:00,694 --> 00:37:03,817
spring will bring
an increase in prey

348
00:37:03,857 --> 00:37:06,139
and her task
will lighten

349
00:37:11,546 --> 00:37:15,231
For all the
inhabitants of this seasonal forest

350
00:37:15,271 --> 00:37:18,754
the long cold
wait is nearly over

351
00:37:31,256 --> 00:37:35,579
Spring in a
deciduous woodland is special

352
00:37:39,342 --> 00:37:41,144
With no
leaves overhead

353
00:37:41,184 --> 00:37:44,546
the rays of the
sun strike the forest floor directly

354
00:37:44,586 --> 00:37:48,389
And their warmth
rouses plants from their winter sleep

355
00:37:56,078 --> 00:37:58,721
The groundliving
plants are in a hurry

356
00:37:58,761 --> 00:38:01,644
Before long the
trees above will come into leaf

357
00:38:01,684 --> 00:38:03,565
and steal
their light

358
00:38:13,655 --> 00:38:16,461
Their flowers
decorate the forest floor

359
00:38:16,501 --> 00:38:18,827
As they advertise
their sweet nectar

360
00:38:18,867 --> 00:38:21,311
To the newly
emerged insects

361
00:38:39,088 --> 00:38:42,050
The spring blooms
of the deciduous woodlands

362
00:38:42,090 --> 00:38:45,732
Have no equivalent in either the great conifer forests

363
00:38:45,772 --> 00:38:47,972
Or the
tropical jungles

364
00:38:53,055 --> 00:38:55,016
Within a
matter of weeks

365
00:38:55,056 --> 00:38:56,977
the canopy
has closed

366
00:38:57,017 --> 00:38:59,939
And only a few
wheeling shafts of light

367
00:38:59,979 --> 00:39:01,819
Penetrate
the woodland

368
00:39:10,499 --> 00:39:11,698
In the treetops

369
00:39:11,738 --> 00:39:15,538
the broad leaves
rapidly expand to their full size

370
00:39:15,578 --> 00:39:18,978
to make the most
of summer while it lasts

371
00:39:25,390 --> 00:39:26,111
Then

372
00:39:26,151 --> 00:39:27,673
after a
few months

373
00:39:27,713 --> 00:39:30,196
the days begin
to shorten again

374
00:39:30,236 --> 00:39:33,400
And the trees
must shut down and shed their leaves

375
00:39:33,440 --> 00:39:37,404
In preparation
for the cold dark time ahead

376
00:39:42,411 --> 00:39:44,774
Great tracts
of North America

377
00:39:44,814 --> 00:39:48,178
flush red as the
season progresses

378
00:39:49,485 --> 00:39:53,967
The effect is so
spectacular and so extensive

379
00:39:54,008 --> 00:39:56,409
that it can be
seen from space

380
00:40:11,948 --> 00:40:13,947
The threat of
winter frost

381
00:40:13,987 --> 00:40:17,986
is not the only
reason for trees to shed leaves

382
00:40:22,630 --> 00:40:25,590
These forests
stand in the tropics

383
00:40:25,790 --> 00:40:26,350
Here

384
00:40:26,390 --> 00:40:28,630
day length
never changes

385
00:40:28,750 --> 00:40:31,070
But the dry
season is so severe

386
00:40:31,110 --> 00:40:33,030
That the trees can
't afford to lose

387
00:40:33,070 --> 00:40:35,391
The amount of
water that would evaporate

388
00:40:35,431 --> 00:40:37,271
From their
broad leaves

389
00:40:37,391 --> 00:40:39,831
So the leaves
must be shed

390
00:40:57,842 --> 00:41:02,605
The forest resembles a European woodland in midwinter

391
00:41:02,845 --> 00:41:05,327
But the heat
is overpowering

392
00:41:05,367 --> 00:41:08,249
and its
inhabitants unfamiliar

393
00:41:12,212 --> 00:41:15,535
For the creatures
of India's teak forests

394
00:41:15,575 --> 00:41:18,016
these are
desperate times

395
00:41:19,458 --> 00:41:21,859
But salvation is at hand

396
00:41:21,939 --> 00:41:24,741
The marwa tree
is about to bloom

397
00:41:29,495 --> 00:41:31,656
Its flowers are
full of liquid

398
00:41:31,696 --> 00:41:33,817
making them
irresistible

399
00:41:40,980 --> 00:41:45,662
The maawah is an
oasis in a hot dry desert

400
00:41:56,337 --> 00:41:58,738
Those that
fly or climb

401
00:41:58,778 --> 00:42:01,780
are not the only
ones to get a share

402
00:42:05,223 --> 00:42:08,585
Chital deer
follow the langur monkeys

403
00:42:08,625 --> 00:42:11,106
collecting the
flowers that fall

404
00:42:17,351 --> 00:42:19,352
The monkeys
welcome the deer

405
00:42:19,392 --> 00:42:23,554
for deer are
unrivalled at spotting predators

406
00:42:25,132 --> 00:42:26,774
If they
are relaxed

407
00:42:26,814 --> 00:42:29,338
it must be safe
to come down to the ground

408
00:42:29,378 --> 00:42:31,900
and gather the
food that lies there

409
00:42:42,795 --> 00:42:47,481
But it's not wise
to travel far from the sentinels

410
00:43:41,194 --> 00:43:43,434
Tropical
Madagascar

411
00:43:43,714 --> 00:43:45,395
The wet season

412
00:43:52,433 --> 00:43:56,438
It's now that the
baobab trees regrow their leaves

413
00:43:56,478 --> 00:44:00,002
and collect water
to store in their huge trunks

414
00:44:00,042 --> 00:44:02,445
ready for the
dry season ahead

415
00:44:23,954 --> 00:44:27,796
The prehistoric
shape of these trees is rightly famous

416
00:44:27,836 --> 00:44:31,518
But few have ever
witnessed the baobab's real magic

417
00:44:31,558 --> 00:44:33,599
For that
happens at night

418
00:44:33,639 --> 00:44:36,040
and high in
the treetops

419
00:44:41,642 --> 00:44:43,203
Flush with water

420
00:44:43,243 --> 00:44:45,684
the baobab
prepares itself

421
00:44:45,724 --> 00:44:48,485
for an unforgettable display

422
00:45:05,693 --> 00:45:07,014
Once started

423
00:45:07,054 --> 00:45:11,736
the footlong flowers can open fully in less than a minute

424
00:45:56,296 --> 00:45:58,337
As the
flowers open

425
00:45:58,377 --> 00:46:01,337
the creatures of
the forest wake

426
00:46:13,141 --> 00:46:17,705
The mouse lemurs
have been hibernating throughout the dry season

427
00:46:17,745 --> 00:46:19,587
With the
return of rains

428
00:46:19,627 --> 00:46:21,789
it's time
to get busy

429
00:46:26,955 --> 00:46:29,478
A dozen share
this tree hole

430
00:46:29,518 --> 00:46:31,400
but there's
plenty of room

431
00:46:31,440 --> 00:46:33,522
The world's
smallest primate

432
00:46:33,562 --> 00:46:35,844
is no bigger
than your hand

433
00:46:41,706 --> 00:46:43,627
High in the
branches above

434
00:46:43,667 --> 00:46:47,108
the beehive's
nectar is starting to flow

435
00:47:01,598 --> 00:47:03,479
A drink of
this sugary

436
00:47:03,519 --> 00:47:05,160
energy
packed liquid

437
00:47:05,200 --> 00:47:07,441
is an ideal way
for the lemurs

438
00:47:07,481 --> 00:47:09,122
to start their day

439
00:47:13,255 --> 00:47:16,417
Liquid oozes from
the flower's centre

440
00:47:16,457 --> 00:47:18,658
and trickles
down the petals

441
00:47:35,067 --> 00:47:38,708
But the nectar is
not intended for lemurs

442
00:47:42,578 --> 00:47:45,262
These
giant hawkmoths

443
00:47:45,302 --> 00:47:48,905
are the drinkers
the tree needs to attract

444
00:47:58,238 --> 00:47:59,560
As they sip

445
00:47:59,600 --> 00:48:01,602
moving from
tree to tree

446
00:48:01,642 --> 00:48:03,765
So they
transfer pollen

447
00:48:03,805 --> 00:48:06,047
and fertilise the flowers

448
00:48:20,296 --> 00:48:24,582
Nectar was an
excellent first course for the lemurs

449
00:48:24,703 --> 00:48:27,626
but moths are
the main dish

450
00:48:29,150 --> 00:48:32,114
The moths are
very important to the lemurs

451
00:48:32,154 --> 00:48:34,678
For they will
replenish the fat reserves

452
00:48:34,718 --> 00:48:38,844
That the lemurs
need to survive the barren dry season

453
00:48:46,928 --> 00:48:50,528
The lemurs might
seem to be a pest for the baobab

454
00:48:50,568 --> 00:48:54,047
They kill its
pollinators and rob it of its nectar

455
00:48:54,087 --> 00:48:57,007
But they do give
something in return

456
00:48:57,047 --> 00:48:59,006
For as they
wrestle with the moths

457
00:48:59,046 --> 00:49:02,765
their fur inevitably becomes dusted with pollen

458
00:49:02,805 --> 00:49:06,205
So they too
become pollinators

459
00:49:28,848 --> 00:49:35,691
As the alternation of wet and dry seasons brings change to some tropical forests

460
00:49:35,731 --> 00:49:42,053
So the progression of summer to winter dictates life in more temperate regions

461
00:49:51,043 --> 00:49:54,687
Whether trees
have needles or broad leaves

462
00:49:54,768 --> 00:49:58,933
It is their
ability to survive annual change

463
00:49:58,974 --> 00:50:00,816
That has
enabled them to cover

464
00:50:00,856 --> 00:50:03,539
Such vast
areas of the earth

465
00:50:03,620 --> 00:50:06,023
And made the
seasonal forests

466
00:50:06,063 --> 00:50:08,906
The greatest
forests of all

